    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50763" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vĕtĕro</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		vetus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make old</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dicendo autem novum veteravit prius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Heb. 8, 13</span></i>
			.—<i>P. a.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vĕ-tĕrātus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>old</i>, <i>inveterate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mederi ulceribus veteratis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					32, 10, 52, § 141</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caseus,</span>”
				<i>mouldy</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Scrib. Comp. 140</span></i>
			.</div>
